<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- What differs per package; the rest is in src/Directory.Build.props -->
    <PackageId>Dahlke.EtherCAT.Diagnostics</PackageId>
    <Description>EtherCAT master and slave diagnostics over TwinCAT ADS — topology scanning, slave and port state, CRC and frame error counters, sync-unit faults, and a change-event stream, read through raw ADS index groups rather than the symbol API.</Description>
    <PackageTags>TwinCAT;ADS;EtherCAT;Beckhoff;PLC;Automation;Diagnostics;Fieldbus</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      The adsify original also granted this to Adsify.Tests, whose fixtures reach in for
      EtherCatClient.BuildPortInfo and EtherCatCache. That grant is dropped here: nothing in this
      repository can build Adsify.Tests, so it would be inert and unverifiable. When adsify switches
      to consuming this as a package, those two sites need either decoupling or the grant restored.
    -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Dahlke.EtherCAT.Diagnostics.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <AdditionalFiles Include="PublicAPI.Shipped.txt" />
    <AdditionalFiles Include="PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../Dahlke.EtherCAT.Esi/Dahlke.EtherCAT.Esi.csproj" />
    <!--
      A ProjectReference now, where the adsify original carried a PackageReference to
      Dahlke.TwinCAT.Ads 0.8.0. That removed SOME of the version pinning the original needed, but
      not all of it — see the Logging.Abstractions note below, which is the half that survives.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="../Dahlke.TwinCAT.Ads/Dahlke.TwinCAT.Ads.csproj" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers" Version="4.14.0">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <!--
      Bracketed to match the ceiling Dahlke.TwinCAT.Ads sets on the same package, so this one cannot
      resolve a Beckhoff version the library it builds on forbids. Why that ceiling exists, and why
      the Microsoft.Extensions references are deliberately NOT bracketed, are in
      Dahlke.TwinCAT.Ads.csproj and Directory.Build.props respectively.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Beckhoff.TwinCAT.Ads" Version="[7.0.292,8.0.0)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" Version="$(MicrosoftExtensionsVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" Version="$(MicrosoftExtensionsVersion)" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions is the ONE reference here that cannot use
    $(MicrosoftExtensionsVersion), and the numbers are deliberately not round. Beckhoff.TwinCAT.Ads
    7.0.292 imposes a transitive FLOOR on it — >= 8.0.3 on net8.0 and >= 10.0.9 on net10.0, read
    from that package's own nuspec dependency groups — and a direct pin below a floor is an NU1605
    downgrade ERROR, not a warning. $(MicrosoftExtensionsVersion) is 8.0.0/9.0.0/10.0.0, so two of
    the three legs fail the build. Measured while adopting this package, not assumed.

    Note what this is NOT: the floors survive the move from a PackageReference to a
    ProjectReference on Dahlke.TwinCAT.Ads, because they come from BECKHOFF rather than from that
    package. The Dahlke-derived floors the adsify original also had to clear (Hosting.Abstractions
    >= 8.0.1, Options >= 8.0.2) did go away with the conversion, which is why those two references
    sit on the shared property above.

    Dahlke.TwinCAT.Ads itself never trips this despite referencing the same Beckhoff package: it
    uses ILogger without declaring Logging.Abstractions directly, so it has no pin to conflict and
    NuGet simply resolves Beckhoff's floor. Declaring it is the more honest thing for a package
    whose public surface takes an ILogger, and the cost is this comment.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="8.0.3" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net9.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="9.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="10.0.9" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
